# ResQ AI — Comprehensive Fix & Architecture Algorithm Reference

**Purpose of this document:** This is a complete, code-free, algorithm-level reference for every fix, design decision, and open item discussed for the ResQ AI project. It exists so that anyone — human or AI — picking up this project can understand *what* needs to change, *why*, *in what order*, and *how* each piece behaves, without needing to read source code first. Every section describes a process: inputs, steps, decision points, outputs, and failure modes — not implementation syntax.

**How to use this document:** Read Section 1 and 2 once, for context. After that, each fix in Sections 3–8 is self-contained — you can jump directly to the fix you're working on. Section 9 covers scope decisions that are not fixes but governance calls. Section 10 is deployment, deliberately parked. Section 11 ties everything together into a build order with dependency reasoning.

